# The containerd release the patch in patches/ applies to, and the one containerd.exe is
# built from.
#
# A tag, not a SHA — unlike packaging/libkrun-windows/UPSTREAM_REV and
# packaging/nerdbox/NERDBOX_REV, which pin unreleased trees where only a SHA is meaningful.
# containerd cuts real releases and the tag is the thing a user would recognise, compare
# against their Linux install, and file a bug against. Tags in containerd are not moved.
#
# v2.3.3 because that is the containerd that nerdbox vendors at
# packaging/nerdbox/NERDBOX_REV. The shim and the daemon share containerd's ttrpc and mount
# types; running a daemon from a different minor than the shim was built against is an extra
# variable nobody needs while the Windows port is still being brought up. If the nerdbox pin
# moves to a nerdbox that vendors a different containerd, move this with it.
v2.3.3
